 ("Economy","A world economy","Trade, privatisation and a Pacific-led boom promised wider opportunity.","The US intelligence outlooks asked how gains, insecurity and international power would be distributed. KPMG added public debt to the equation.","When do political rivalry, fiscal limits and concentrated ownership outweigh the efficiencies of integration?"),
 ("Environment","From background to boundary","The environment had little space among Naisbitt’s ten headlines. Environmental scholarship already had a long history outside that list.","Resource productivity and biodiversity loss gained explicit places in CSIRO’s 2012 set. Later reports treated adaptation as a condition for continued settlement and livelihoods.","Which places can afford to adapt, which losses can be avoided, and who chooses where to retreat?"),
